//BUG="a template instance may fall off the end"
//ERR any

// A template is checked once per instance, after its types are known. The body
// here is missing a return whatever `T` turns out to be, so the instance for
// i32 has to be rejected — and the diagnostic has to survive being reported
// from inside an instantiation rather than from a plain declaration.

fn pick[T] x: T flag
    if flag
        ret x

fn main
    out "{pick[i32](5 false)}"
